reply.body:
I was able to find the issue, so I'll add it here for anyone else who might have a similar problem.

```
        @Override
        protected void setResource(PaletteBitmap resource) {
            view.setImageBitmap(resource.bitmap);
        }
```

I had originally moved this line of code to `onResourceReady()` since it was crashing the app in `setResource()` due to occasional null values. It had also broken the animation but I didn't notice that until recently. I realized this might be the issue since it was in your code snippet above, so I added it back with a null check before trying to set the bitmap. This ended up fixing the issue while keeping the animation. I'm still not sure why it will sometimes be null, but that's a problem for another day.

